WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.541
Virtual memory gives a process an address space whose addresses are translated to physical memory.

00:00:05.541 --> 00:00:10.342
Paging divides that address space into equal-sized pages and physical memory into frames.

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:13.298
A page table records mappings and access permissions.

00:00:13.298 --> 00:00:17.730
Virtual memory is more than a synonym for a disk swap file.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:26.414
2500 = 2×1024 + 452, so the page is 2 and the offset is 452.

00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:31.025
The physical address is 7×1024 + 452 = 7620.

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:36.660
This example assumes the entry is present and permits the access.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.429
Which part is unchanged by this translation?

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:44.385
The offset identifies the same position within the selected frame.
